  "result": "The gate passed with **OK** on NRS_484B_450_1k: all 12 witnesses gave their expected verdicts, using 3 of the 6 gate runs.\n\n**How the rule is split:** the rule follows where the node's own fields put things.\n- **Applicability (when the rule applies):** the subject is a vehicle stopped alongside or across from an obstruction on a highway it occupies, and the halt would obstruct traffic. That means the body is less than `p.free_passage_width` from the obstruction, and no road edge on the other side is at least that far away.\n- **Obligation (what it requires):** the vehicle must not be at rest, unless one of these exceptions holds:\n  - another member of traffic is ahead in the same lane within `p.queue_halt_gap`;\n  - the lane the vehicle occupies is governed by a stop sign, a yield sign, a red traffic signal, an active railway crossing signal or gate, or a police officer directing a stop.\n\n**One choice the node left open:** the node's \"in compliance with law\" exception (s5: stop sign, red signal) is fully contained in its traffic-control-device exception (s7). I wrote the two once, as a single list of devices, so the same tests aren't repeated. The meaning is unchanged, and I declared no narrowings.\n\n**Gate runs:**\n1. **UNUSED_CLAIM**, from running the gate on the untouched skeleton by mistake.\n2. **CHECK_FAIL** on units: I tested \"opposite side\" as the product of the two lateral offsets being below zero, and compared it with a zero in metres. I fixed it by comparing with zero metres times zero metres.\n3. **OK**.\n\nI also tried a `--help` call to the gate as an extra command. Permissions blocked it and it never ran.\n\n**Extra scenarios:** besides the six planned ones, I added six that should pass (`branch_3` to `branch_8`), so that every exception is tested at least once:\n- stop sign;\n- yield sign;\n- red signal;\n- railway lights flashing;\n- railway gate down;\n- a vehicle stopped 2 m ahead in the same lane.\n\nI found nothing wrong with the node or with the halt concept it uses. Files are in `/scratch/fsw/portfolios/av/projects/av_alpamayo_reasoning/users/wcong/WorldModelSpec/.worktrees/full221-v2/pipeline/traffic-spec-agent/`:\n- `library/TrafficSpec/Rules/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_450_1k.lean`\n- `library/TrafficSpecWitness/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_450_1k.lean`\n- `results/full221-1116-1018/iter-002/code/NRS_484B_450_1k/task_result.md`",
